{
  "version": "4",
  "notes": "The guided curriculum schedule — editable independently of the app. Three tiers (docs/lessons.md): `units` are themed worlds (emoji landmarks on the home strip); each unit's `levels` are its sub-levels (rooms); each level's `lessons` are the bite-sized nodes on the path. A level `introduce`s a small core glyph set (empty = a review room), lists the `games` its themed lessons draw from, and flags `story` where stories.v1.json has an unlocked tale (Story Time node). Symbol pool at level N = union of `introduce` over 1..N; every symbol gets a Meet card + drill block before games use it. Teaching levels run 4 nodes (meet → sounds → story → reading), review rooms 3 (sounds → story → reading) — deliberately unhurried. `xpToAdvance` is retained for the decoupled rewards layer. Game ids: listen_and_pick, find_the_character, picture_to_word, symbol_hunt, hidden_glyph, feed_the_guide, sound_match, families, echo_read, story_time, build_a_word, blend_reveal, build_a_sentence, fill_blank.",
